  chaptersLead: `<p>Pride and Prejudice was published in three volumes and is still organized by them. Volume 1 (Chapters 1–23) establishes the world and ends with the Collins proposal and Elizabeth's refusal. Volume 2 (Chapters 24–42) takes Elizabeth to Hunsford and Rosings, brings Darcy's catastrophic first proposal in Chapter 34, and his letter the next morning — the hinge of the whole novel. Volume 3 (Chapters 43–61) begins at Pemberley and ends with two weddings in the same week.</p>`,
